{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":73475847,"ns":0,"title":"Vietoris–Rips filtration","extract":"In topological data analysis, the Vietoris–Rips filtration (sometimes shortened to \"Rips filtration\") is the collection of nested Vietoris–Rips complexes on a metric space created by taking the sequence of Vietoris–Rips complexes over an increasing scale parameter. Often, the Vietoris–Rips filtration is used to create a discrete, simplicial model on point cloud data embedded in an ambient metric space.","description":"Topological data analysis tool","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}